<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Greece and the Aegean</p><h1 class="st-title">Epirote League</h1><p class="st-meta">232 BCE – 167 BCE · capital Phoenice</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Federal republic of the peoples of Epirus that replaced the Aeacid monarchy and ended in mass enslavement by Rome in 167 BCE.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Around 232 BCE the last of the royal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aeacidae">Aeacid</a> family, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deidamia-ii-of-epirus">Deidamia</a>, was killed and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/molossians">Molossians</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chaonians">Chaonians</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thesprotians">Thesprotians</a> abolished the monarchy of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-epirus">Kingdom of Epirus</a>. They formed a federal state, the Koinon of the Epirotes, whose meetings were often held at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phoenice">Phoenice</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chaonia">Chaonia</a>, near the Ionian coast.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The league was led by annually elected generals and a federal assembly, and minted coins showing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zeus">Zeus</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dione">Dione of Dodona</a>. Its regions remained distinct, and wealth came from herding and trade with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>. Illyrian raiders under Queen <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teuta">Teuta</a> sacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phoenice">Phoenice</a> in 230 BCE. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peace-of-phoenice">Peace of Phoenice</a>, ending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-macedonian-war">First Macedonian War</a> in 205 BCE, was signed there.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-macedonian-war">Third Macedonian War</a> the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/molossians">Molossians</a> sided with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/perseus-of-macedon">Perseus</a> while other Epirotes supported <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>. In 167 BCE the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/commune-of-rome">Roman Senate</a> ordered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lucius-aemilius-paullus-macedonicus">Lucius Aemilius Paullus</a> to punish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/epirus">Epirus</a>: seventy towns were plundered and about 150,000 people enslaved, ending the league.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/epirote-league.jpg" alt="Epirote League" width="320" height="162"><figcaption>Image: CNG · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Epirus234bc.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>232 BCE – 167 BCE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Phoenice</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Ancient Greek religion (cult of Zeus at Dodona)</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Ancient Greek (North-West Greek)</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/greece">Greece</a>, <a href="/countries/albania">Albania</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Koinon of the Epirotes</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-200&amp;focus=epirote-league" aria-label="Epirote League on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5174 749 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Epirote League lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5494 1005L5519 1030M5494 1005L5304 942"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5519 1030h0M5304 942h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5494 1005h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5494 1005h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Phoenice. <a href="/atlas?year=-200&amp;focus=epirote-league">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
